Task 1: Spring Boot Data JPA – Employee Resume Management System (CLOB)
Scenario
Develop a Spring Boot application for an HR Management System where employee resumes need
to be stored in the database. Since resumes can contain large amounts of text data, store them
using CLOB.
Entity Class: EmployeeResume
employeeId : Long
employeeName : String
designation : String
resumeContent : String (CLOB)
Requirements
Entity Layer- Create an entity class named EmployeeResume.- Use @Entity and @Table.- Mark employeeId as primary key using @Id.- Store resumeContent using:
@Lob
@Column(columnDefinition = "CLOB")
private String resumeContent;
Repository Layer
Create EmployeeResumeRepository extending:
JpaRepository<EmployeeResume, Long>
Service Layer
Implement methods:
1. Save Employee Resume
2. View Employee Resume by Id
3. View All Employee Resumes
4. Delete Employee Resume
Runner Class
Using CommandLineRunner:- Insert 3 employee resumes.- Fetch and display all employee resumes.- Retrieve a resume using employee id.- Delete one employee record.
Expected Output
Employee Resume Saved Successfully
Employee Id : 101
Employee Name : John
Designation : Java Developer
Resume Content : Experienced Java Developer with 5 years of experience...
Employee Resume Deleted Successfull